# README models table

## Row order

In [README.md](../README.md) `## Models`, sort table rows by **LiveCodeBench v6 score descending** (highest first).

When adding or updating a model row, re-sort the full table. Ties: keep stable order or sort by model name.

LiveCodeBench values come from official vendor model cards (see table footnote). Update the score and month on the row when the source changes.

## Footnote

Keep the paragraph under the table (LiveCodeBench source, quant vs BF16 note, [gguf-bench](https://gguf-bench.com/) link). Do not remove when reordering rows.

## Adding a model

Scaffold under `models/{model}/` per create-model-configs. On scaffold, add the README row at the correct LiveCodeBench rank (lookup v6 on the vendor model card; do not run calibration). Use **TODO** for throughput, est. context, VRAM/RAM, and disk until `./tester_v1_calibrate.py` results exist; fill max context from the model spec when known. Re-sort by score; do not append by default. Replace TODOs after the user runs calibration.
